<section class="story-hero wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">Rooted in the earth. Made for you.</p><h1>Old wisdom.<br>Everyday <em>goodness.</em></h1><p>Oorvi means earth. For us, it’s also a reminder: the best things in our kitchen begin with nature, and don’t need much else.</p><p>From the heart of Hyderabad, we’re bringing traditional pressing back to the everyday. One seed. One pressing. One honest bottle.</p></div><img src="{{ 'oorvi-hero-v4.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Oorvi groundnut and coconut oils on sunlit stone" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high"></section>
<section class="story-manifesto wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Our simple belief</p><h2>Goodness isn’t something<br>you add. It’s something <em>you keep.</em></h2><p>The flavour of the seed. The care in the process. The comfort of a familiar meal. We make oils that bring all three together.</p></section>
<section class="story-chapter wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Back to the basics</p><h2>Good seeds.<br>A good <em>beginning.</em></h2></div><div><p>It starts with carefully chosen native seeds. Groundnut, sesame, sunflower, safflower, mustard, and coconut each bring their own character to your cooking.</p><p>We don’t blend our oils to make them all taste the same. A nutty aroma, a distinctive colour, or a little natural sediment is part of what makes each bottle its own.</p></div></section>
<section class="story-chapter wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / The first & only press</p><h2>Slow is<br><em>our way.</em></h2></div><div><p>Our cold pressed range uses a steel expeller. Our wood pressed range follows the traditional slow-turning ghani method. Every oil is single pressed, without refining, bleaching, or deodorising.</p><p>Then we let it settle naturally. There’s no extra step to strip away its colour or aroma. Just oil with the character of the seed it came from.</p></div></section>
